# Task: Fix VACE Tab UI — Wrong Bindings & Missing Chunk Progress

## 1. Context & Objective

The Video Generator window VACE tab shows stale MainVM log data ("Video Generator initialized / Workflow changed to: Painter...") instead of VACE processing output. The progress bar and status text also don't update during chunk generation because the XAML binds to generic `ProcessingStatus`/`ProcessingProgress`/`LogOutput` aliases that resolve to `MainVM`, not `VaceVM`.

Additionally, the VACE tab has no chunk counter UI (unlike the Mocha tab which correctly shows "X chunks"), and several result-section bindings (video player, buttons, info text) also point to MainVM properties.

**Two files need changes:**
1. `FlipPix.UI/ViewModels/VideoGeneratorViewModel.cs` — add missing pass-through properties
2. `FlipPix.UI/VideoGeneratorWindow.xaml` — fix all wrong bindings and add chunk counter

---

## 2. Files to Modify

### File A: `FlipPix.UI/ViewModels/VideoGeneratorViewModel.cs`

In the `#region VaceVM Backward Compatibility Properties` section (around line 280), add these **missing** pass-through properties (do not change existing ones):

```csharp
public int VaceTotalFrames => VaceVM.TotalFrames;
public int VaceTotalChunks => VaceVM.TotalChunks;
public string VaceProgressPercentage => VaceVM.ProgressPercentage;
public string VaceResultVideoInfo => VaceVM.ResultVideoInfo;
```

### File B: `FlipPix.UI/VideoGeneratorWindow.xaml`

#### Fix 1 — Processing status block (around lines 1369–1383)

Replace the three bindings inside the `IsProcessingVACE` Border:

| Old binding | New binding |
|---|---|
| `{Binding ProcessingStatus}` | `{Binding VaceProcessingStatus}` |
| `{Binding ProcessingProgress}` | `{Binding VaceProcessingProgress}` |
| `{Binding ProgressPercentage}` | `{Binding VaceProgressPercentage}` |

Also add a chunk-counter TextBlock **before** the progress bar (modelled on the Mocha tab, which uses `MochaTotalChunks`):

```xml
<TextBlock HorizontalAlignment="Center"
           FontSize="11"
           Foreground="#FF6B35"
           Margin="0,0,0,5">
    <Run Text="Chunks: "/>
    <Run Text="{Binding VaceTotalChunks, Mode=OneWay}" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
    <Run Text=" × 81 frames"/>
</TextBlock>
```

Place it between the status TextBlock and the ProgressBar.

#### Fix 2 — Result video section (around lines 1395–1458)

| Old binding | New binding |
|---|---|
| `{Binding HasResultVideo}` (DataTrigger, line ~1408) | `{Binding HasVACEResult}` |
| `{Binding HasResultVideo}` (MediaElement Visibility, line ~1422) | `{Binding HasVACEResult}` |
| `{Binding ResultVideoPath}` (MediaElement Source, line ~1418) | `{Binding VaceResultPath}` |
| `IsEnabled="{Binding HasResultVideo}"` (Play button, ~1437) | `IsEnabled="{Binding HasVACEResult}"` |
| `Command="{Binding PlayVideoCommand}"` (~1436) | `Command="{Binding PlayVACEVideoCommand}"` |
| `IsEnabled="{Binding HasResultVideo}"` (Open Folder button, ~1444) | `IsEnabled="{Binding HasVACEResult}"` |
| `Command="{Binding OpenResultFolderCommand}"` (~1443) | `Command="{Binding OpenVACEResultFolderCommand}"` |
| `IsEnabled="{Binding HasResultVideo}"` (Send to Edit Camera, ~1451) | `IsEnabled="{Binding HasVACEResult}"` |
| `{Binding VideoInfo}` (info text, ~1454) | `{Binding VaceResultVideoInfo}` |

#### Fix 3 — Log section (around line 1472)

| Old binding | New binding |
|---|---|
| `{Binding LogOutput, Mode=OneWay}` | `{Binding VaceLogOutput, Mode=OneWay}` |

---

## 3. Implementation Steps

1. Open `VideoGeneratorViewModel.cs`, locate `#region VaceVM Backward Compatibility Properties`, add the 4 new pass-through properties after the existing `IsAnalyzingVACE` line.
2. Open `VideoGeneratorWindow.xaml`:
   a. Find the `IsProcessingVACE` Border block and replace the 3 bindings + insert the chunk counter TextBlock.
   b. Find the Result Video section and apply all 9 binding replacements (table in Fix 2).
   c. Find the VACE log `TextBox` and change `LogOutput` → `VaceLogOutput`.
3. Do NOT change anything outside the VACE tab section or the VaceVM region in the ViewModel.

---

## 4. Completion Instructions

Update this file with a "Changelog" section detailing every line changed.

---

